<title>CONGO: IMF team visits Congo, spotlight on civil service.</title>
<headline>IMF team visits Congo, spotlight on civil service.</headline>
<dateline>BRAZZAVILLE 1996-11-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>An International Monetary Fund (IMF) team has arrived in Congo to investigate government compliance with promises made as part of a three-year funding agreement struck earlier this year, officials said.</p>
<p>Under the Enhanced Structural Adjustment Facility accord, signed three months ago, the government agreed to cut the state salary bill by laying off 9,000 of the 70,000 civil servants by 1999.</p>
<p>The IMF team, which arrived on Friday, will also examine progress towards privatisation of state companies.</p>
</text>
